{
  "name": "TextKindIsText",
  "comment": "Stage 1 (decision 867): text's face without the name floor. `source.cs:115` today reads\n`_type.kind.IsText || _type.Name is \"text\"` — the Name fallback is only there because\na kind built inline from a name (`type/this.cs:149`) answers `IsText=false` even for a\ntext's own kind. When the type is born whole, the registered md kind carries\n`Text = true` (its mime `text/markdown` begins with `text/`), so `kind.istext` alone\nanswers; the Name floor can go. Red on runtime2: today the fresh `kind.@this(\"md\")`\nhas `_text = false`, so `%x!type.kind.istext%` reads false (expected true).",
